    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Aero MinI COLLECTOR SERIES\nREAL WORKING PARTS\nAUTHENTIC SCALE\nDIE CAST METAL\nBOEING 737-200",
      "Boeing 737-200\n\"Commuter\"\nOne of the newest of the short haul \"commuter\" air-\nplanes, the Boeing 737-200 entered scheduled airline\nservice in August 1967.\nThe Boeing 737 is the only one of the leading short\nhaul airplanes to utilize engines mounted convention-\nally in pods under the wings. It is designed to operate\neconomically on flights of 1,000 to 1,500 miles and\nutilizes many of the components and assemblies of the\nlarger Boeing 727: the fuselage structure is basically\nthe same with identical doors, side panels and interior\nappointments. Engines and mechanical systems are\nalso similar.\nAlthough the fuselage of the 737 is only 96 feet long,\nit can accommodate a 16-ton payload, and seating is\nprovided for 88 to 113 passengers. The 737 owes its\nexcellent small field performance to a combination of\nKrueger leading edge flaps and Boeing-developed\ntriple-slotted trailing edge flaps.\nThe 737-200 is equipped with two Pratt \u0026 Whitney\nJT8D-9 Turbofan engines of 14,500 Ibs. thrust each\nand cruises at 573 m.p.h. Range at a maximum gross\nweight of 107,000 Ibs. is 2,400 miles.\n93 FT\n100 FT\nAero Mini's Collectors Series models are authentically detailed miniature reproductions of the world's most famous\nairplanes. Models are of all-metal construction and precision die cast to an accuracy of five thousands of an inch.\nLanding gear and passenger loading stairways can be raised or lowered to simulate in-flight or on-ground appear-\nance. Each model carries the official identification of one of the world's leading airlines. Built with the accuracy and\nprecision of collectors' demands, these models are rugged enough for everyday play.\nOther exciting models in the\nAero Mini Collectors Series of World-Famous Commercial Airliners:\nB.A.C. Super VC-10\nBoeing 727-100\n\"Tri-Jet\"\nBoeing 747\nDouglas DC-8-61\n\"Jumbo Jet\"\n\"Stretch Jet\"\nBoeing 707-320B\n\"Intercontinental\"\nDouglas DC-9 Sr. 10\nBoeing SST\nLockheed L-1011\n\"Inter-City\"\n\"Supersonic Jet\"\n\"Air Bus\"\nThis handsome all metal desk-top display stand is adaptable to all Aero Mini models:\nAero Mini® Incorporated 115 Schmitt Boulevard, Farmingdale, New York 11735, U.S.A.\nS-100\nDisplay Stand\nManufactured in Japan\nPrinted in U.S. A."
    ],
